  jp morgan the wall street bank has put  together  a loan package of worth about six  billion  dollars to finance the launch of the  european premier league now this would  be money that would be repayable from  future broadcast six billion dollars  being 4.6 billion pounds so it would be  one of the richest  team tournaments in the world of sport  as i say this could get announced in the  next couple of weeks but key  details are still to be finalized and  given the fraught  politics in football at the moment bear  in mind that just in the last couple of  weeks  in english football the political  landscape has fractured very  significantly  between the project big pitch over broad  project big picture  which was the initiative that was  proposed by liverpool and manchester  united  uh to reduce the number of teams in the  premier league  given this fracturing landscape there  has to be some doubt about whether this  new european premier league  will get off the ground but what we can  say for certain is that those talks are  underway  and they are at an advanced stage with  an announcement possible  as soon as the next few weeks
 

